WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
<v Alicia Kwan>Good morning everyone, let's start the Architecture Alignment Council. Today we're covering the Azure Data Lake Migration status.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
<v Jordan Reyes>Thanks Alicia. Infrastructure has finished the initial VPC setup, but we're still blocked on the SOC2 vendor exception for the Azure storage module.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Alicia Kwan>Understood. Let's approve the cloud migration budget of 480,000 dollars for this quarter so the team isn't blocked on funding while Security finishes the review.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Priya Shah>I'll take the SOC2 vendor exception review. Security will have a decision back to the group by next Friday.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Jordan Reyes>On process — once a new vendor request comes in, here's how it flows today. First, the requesting team submits the vendor intake form. Then Procurement does an initial screen for completeness.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:08.000
<v Jordan Reyes>If it passes screening, Security runs the SOC2 and HIPAA review in parallel with Legal's contract review. If either one rejects it, the request goes back to the requesting team with comments.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:20.000
<v Jordan Reyes>If both Security and Legal approve, Procurement finalizes the vendor record and notifies the requesting team that the vendor is cleared to use.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
<v Alicia Kwan>Good overview, thanks Jordan. Finance, can you confirm the budget breakdown by next week's session?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
<v Marcus Lee>Finance will confirm the budget breakdown by our next session.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:46.000
<v Alicia Kwan>Great. Let's circulate the previous minutes of meeting to the full group before we close. EPMO, can you own that?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.000
<v Priya Shah>EPMO already circulated the previous MoM yesterday, that one's done.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
<v Alicia Kwan>Perfect, thanks everyone. That wraps up today's council. See you all next week.
